          "title": "Products Products of of Research Research",
          "description": null,
          "order": 1,
          "question": [
            {
              "id": 1,
              "text": "Products Products of of Research Research",
              "order": 1,
              "answer": {
                "id": 1,
                "json": {
                  "type": "textArea",
                  "meta": {
                    "schemaVersion": "1.0"
                  },
                  "answer": "Battery material samples will be synthesized in powder form and identified through a consistent and systematic labeling procedure, which will include sample composition, name of researcher and date. Experimental data generated over the course of the research will include synthesis procedures and results from characterization of battery electrode samples."
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Data Data Format Format Standards Standards",
          "description": null,
          "order": 2,
          "question": [
            {
              "id": 2,
              "text": "Data Data Format Format Standards Standards",
              "order": 1,
              "answer": {
                "id": 2,
                "json": {
                  "type": "textArea",
                  "meta": {
                    "schemaVersion": "1.0"
                  },
                  "answer": "In order to allow for interoperability, reproducibility, and reuse, all data will be stored and saved in standard and open formats. Experimental characterization data will be stored and saved as, e.g., ASCII, CSV, Word, Matlab and Python files."
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": 3,
              "text": "Crystallographic data",
              "order": 2,
              "answer": {
                "id": 3,
                "json": {
                  "type": "textArea",
                  "meta": {
                    "schemaVersion": "1.0"
                  },
                  "answer": "Crystallographic data will be reported in standard crystallographic information framework (*.cif) format to facilitate visualization and further analysis through widely available software tools (VESTA, cif2file, etc.). Crystallographic data for previously-unreported compounds/structures will be uploaded to the ICSD database."
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
